From 6105eb9a2c6beb24b8630055a73db5b834d1aa71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:23:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] panvk: use INTERSECT ZS preload on v9 and v10 too

csf-v11/061 switched the v11 Z/S preload frame shader from
EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS to INTERSECT; v9 (G78, JM) and v10 (G710/G610, CSF)
kept the upstream EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS mode, which reads Z/S for every tile
of a pass that loads depth/stencil, including tiles no primitive
touches: up to 10.4 MB of Z plus 2.6 MB of S per pass at 2400x1080.

INTERSECT is safe for the same reason it is for the colour preload,
which already uses it on every arch: a load target that is not
`always` is not written back for tiles without primitives, so skipping
the preload for those tiles changes nothing in memory.  A target that
must be written for empty tiles (a CLEAR in-bounds load with a border
load, always_load()) still gets EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS.  v12 keeps
EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS and v13+ keeps PREPASS_ALWAYS.

Rationale: perf review 2026-10-26 C6 ("v9/v10 still preload Z/S on
every tile; 061 changed only v11").  Knob: PANVK_ZS_PRELOAD_ALWAYS=1
restores EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS on v9-v11 (the 114 behaviour for v9/v10); it
is the existing 061 knob, read once and cached by
DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c
index 31be72d2..4ca5545d 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_frame_shaders.c
@@ -795,7 +795,7 @@ always_load(const struct pan_fb_load *load,
           (pan_fb_shader_key_target_written(&key->key.s) && load->s.always);
 }
 
-#if PAN_ARCH == 11
+#if PAN_ARCH >= 9 && PAN_ARCH <= 11
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION(zs_preload_always, "PANVK_ZS_PRELOAD_ALWAYS", false)
 #endif
 
@@ -823,18 +823,18 @@ cmd_preload_zs_attachments(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       return result;
 
-   /* We could use INTERSECT on Valhall too, but EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS has the
-    * advantage of reloading the ZS tile buffer one or more tiles ahead,
-    * making ZS data immediately available for any ZS tests taking place in
-    * other shaders.  Thing's haven't been benchmarked to determine what's
-    * preferable (saving bandwidth vs having ZS preloaded earlier), so let's
-    * leave it like that for now.
+   /* EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS reloads the ZS tile buffer one or more tiles ahead,
+    * making ZS data immediately available for ZS tests in other shaders,
+    * but it reads Z/S for every tile, including tiles no primitive touches.
+    * On v9-v11 use INTERSECT, like the colour preload, unless the target
+    * has to be written for empty tiles too (always_load()).
+    * PANVK_ZS_PRELOAD_ALWAYS=1 restores EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS.
     *
     * On v13+, we don't have EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS instead we use PREPASS_ALWAYS.
     */
 #if PAN_ARCH >= 13
    fs->modes[dcd_idx] = MALI_PRE_POST_FRAME_SHADER_MODE_PREPASS_ALWAYS;
-#elif PAN_ARCH == 11
+#elif PAN_ARCH >= 9 && PAN_ARCH <= 11
    fs->modes[dcd_idx] = (always_load(load, &key) ||
                          debug_get_option_zs_preload_always())
                         ? MALI_PRE_POST_FRAME_SHADER_MODE_EARLY_ZS_ALWAYS
-- 
2.55.0

